  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 102 PM MDT Mon Oct 19 2026\n\nDeep southerly flow aloft setting in today through Thursday\nwhich will allow some moisture to return to southeast Idaho.\nWill see isolated mainly high elevation showers and\nthunderstorms Tuesday and Wednesday. As upper level low pressure\napproaches will see widespread rain both Thursday and Friday.\nMost areas around a 50 percent chance over 0.5 inches of\nprecipitation. Snow levels drop to 7 to 8 thousand feet on\nFriday with at least a chance of accumulation above that level.\nLow elevation highs will be around 70 Tuesday through Thursday\nwith mountains mid 50s to mid 60s. On Friday expect highs in the\nupper 30s to 40s mountains and 40s to around 50 valleys. By\nSunday and Monday will rise to near normal in the 40s and 50s\nmountains and 50s to around 60 valleys.",
